From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pm: let microG present Google's certificate on user builds

LineageOS answers a package-info query for com.google.android.gms and
com.android.vending with Google's certificate in both signatures and
signingInfo, but only for a package that is signed by microG's release
key alone and carries that certificate as its fake-signature meta-data
(ComputerEngine.isMicrogSigned). The method also required
isDebuggable(), a compile-time property of the build, so the spoof was
off on every user build.

The check is removed, as lineageos4microg's user-build patch does.
What is left decides as before: the two package names, the exact
signer and the exact meta-data value. No permission or API is added,
and a package with another signer is never spoofed, whatever its name.
The native isDebuggable() stays: the WebView update service calls it.
---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
index 4e499dcc6f0a5c7b9b063ee1e3b2f6f610a70b75..ef242abde3f88af378d4a9752b84d9bdb7a0e8cd 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/ComputerEngine.java
@@ -1492,9 +1492,7 @@ public class ComputerEngine implements Computer {
     public static native boolean isDebuggable();
 
     public static boolean isMicrogSigned(AndroidPackage p) {
-        if (!isDebuggable()) {
-            return false;
-        }
+        // Not limited to debuggable builds: the package name and the exact signer decide.
 
         // Allowlist the following apps:
         // * com.android.vending - microG Companion
